---
description: Review the actual owned System candidate and fulfil the requested comparison or private handoff.
args:
  goal: string
returns: SystemCandidateOutcome
---
Determine what the requested review needs from the current candidate and its actual file evidence. Compose the discovery, evidence interpretation, currentness and handoff functions according to what they return. Distinguish a comparison answer from a requested private diagnosis; an allowed local note is not an instruction to create one for every query.

Use the actual local, incoming and common-basis bytes to explain compatibility, convergence, deletion or uncertainty. A changed frontier invalidates the earlier write basis; it does not establish a new candidate or authorize an automatic retry. Retain only an actually authorized handoff, interpret a refused operation honestly, and return its real reference or the requested supported finding. Preserve protected main and unrelated files; this computation has no merge, publication or rollout authority.
